  "body": "# 117 — Tennessine\n\n```yaml\nmat_id: \"MAT:0117\"\nrecord_name: \"Tennessine\"\nsymbol: \"Ts\"\natomic_number: 117\nrecord_class: CHEMICAL_ELEMENT\nparent_id: \"MAT:0000\"\nschema_version: \"1.0.0\"\nrecord_version: \"1.0.0\"\nstatus: BASELINE\ncreated: \"2026-09-08\"\nupdated: \"2026-09-08\"\ncontributors: []\n```\n\n---\n\n# 0. Record Navigation\n\n## Parent\n\nMAT:0000 — Origin State\n\n## Child Records\n\n[Evaluated nuclear states](0117-Tennessine-Ts-Nuclear-Evaluation.md) · source evaluation and structured isotope data.\n\n## Related Records\n\nNone yet.\n\n---\n\n# 1. Identity\n\n| Field | Value | Unit / Status | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Canonical name | Tennessine | | IUPAC |\n| Symbol | Ts | | IUPAC |\n| Record class | CHEMICAL_ELEMENT | | MAT |\n| Atomic number | 117 | | IUPAC |\n| Standard atomic weight | NOT_APPLICABLE | NOT_APPLICABLE | CIAAW-2024 |\n| Period | 7 | | IUPAC |\n| Group | 17 | | IUPAC |\n| Block | p | | IUPAC |\n| Category | Halogen | | IUPAC |\n\n---\n\n# 2. Executive Scientific Summary\n\nTennessine (Ts, Z = 117) is a halogen in period 7, group 17 of the periodic table.\n\n**Status:** Baseline element record — awaiting curated MAT expansion.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Natural State and Manifestation\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V01 -->\n<!-- ASSET-ID: MAT:0117:FIG:V01:001 -->\n<!-- STATUS: SOURCE-IMAGE-REQUIRED -->\n```\n\nDescribe physical state, appearance, occurrence.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Conventional Scientific Representation\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V02 -->\n```\n\nInclude symbol, atomic/molecular representation.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Atomic / Molecular / Crystal Structure\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V03 -->\n```\n\nBond network, coordination, lattice, space group.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Quantum and Electronic Structure\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V04 -->\n```\n\nElectronic configuration: **[Rn]7s2 7p5 5f14 6d10 (predicted)** (PREDICTED; PUBCHEM-PERIODIC).\n\n---\n\n# 7. Isotopes and Nuclear States\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V05 -->\n```\n\n[Evaluated nuclear states](0117-Tennessine-Ts-Nuclear-Evaluation.md) provides 4 states from NUBASE2020, including ground states and separately indexed excited states. The linked table preserves half-lives, uncertainties, qualifiers and source lines. Later measurements and wider nuclear research still require review.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Spectra, Frequency and Resonance\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V06 -->\n```\n\nElectronic, vibrational, rotational, Raman, hyperfine, nuclear, magnetic resonance, acoustic, plasma.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Physical Properties\n\n| Property | Value | Unit | Conditions | Evidence | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| atomicWeight | NOT_APPLICABLE | dimensionless / text | See source | NOT_APPLICABLE | CIAAW-2024 |\n| electronConfiguration | [Rn]7s2 7p5 5f14 6d10 (predicted) | dimensionless / text | See source | PREDICTED | PUBCHEM-PERIODIC |\n| electronegativity | UNAVAILABLE | Pauling | See source | UNAVAILABLE | UNAVAILABLE |\n| firstIonizationEnergy | UNAVAILABLE | eV | See source | UNAVAILABLE | UNAVAILABLE |\n| phase | UNKNOWN | dimensionless / text | See source | UNKNOWN | UNAVAILABLE |\n| meltingPoint | UNAVAILABLE | K | See source | UNAVAILABLE | UNAVAILABLE |\n| boilingPoint | UNAVAILABLE | K | See source | UNAVAILABLE | UNAVAILABLE |\n| density | UNAVAILABLE | g/cm3 | See source | UNAVAILABLE | UNAVAILABLE |\n| oxidationStates | +5, +3, +1, -1 | dimensionless / text | See source | PREDICTED | PUBCHEM-PERIODIC |\n\nAbundances remain UNAVAILABLE pending source-specific curation. Standard atomic weight is dimensionless; isotope mass numbers are not substituted for it. For helium, a melting point needs pressure-specific qualification.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Electrical Properties\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V08 -->\n```\n\nConductivity, resistivity, permittivity, dielectric loss.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Magnetic Properties\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V09 -->\n```\n\nSusceptibility, ordering, permeability, magnetic moments.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Thermal and Thermodynamic Properties\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V10 -->\n```\n\nMelting, boiling, heat capacity, conductivity, diffusivity.\n\n---\n\n# 13. Mechanical Properties\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V11 -->\n```\n\nModulus, strength, hardness, toughness, creep, fatigue.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Phase, Pressure and Environment\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V12 -->\n```\n\nPhase transitions, pressure dependence, environmental stability.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Chemical Behaviour\n\nOxidation states, common bonding, reactivity, redox, acids/bases, corrosion, solubility.\n\n---\n\n# 16. Compounds and Materials\n\n```text\nFORMS-COMPOUND\nCONSTITUENT-OF\nFORMS-ALLOTROPE\nUSED-IN-MATERIAL\n```\n\n---\n\n# 17. Processes and Transformations\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V13 -->\n```\n\n---\n\n# 18. Energy\n\nGeneration, storage, transport, conversion.\n\n---\n\n# 19. Biological Context\n\nScientifically supported biological relationships only.\n\n---\n\n# 20. Environment and Sustainability\n\nOccurrence, extraction, abundance, recycling, environmental fate, supply risk.\n\n---\n\n# 21. Applications\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V17 -->\n```\n\n```text\nCOMMERCIAL\nDEMONSTRATED\nRESEARCH\nPROPOSED\nHYPOTHETICAL\n```\n\n---\n\n# 22. Safety\n\nChemical, thermal, pressure, electrical, magnetic, radiation, biological, environmental hazards.\n\n---\n\n# 23. Time Dependence\n\nDecay, ageing, corrosion, fatigue, relaxation, degradation.\n\n---\n\n# 24. Scale Dependence\n\n```text\nATOMIC\nMOLECULAR\nNANO\nMICRO\nMACRO\nBULK\n```\n\n---\n\n# 25. Geometry Effects\n\nThickness, orientation, shape, surface area, topology.\n\n---\n\n# 26. Relationships\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V14 -->\n```\n\n---\n\n# 27. Scientific 3D Model\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V15 -->\n```\n\n---\n\n# 28. MAT Data-Extruded 3D Model\n\n```html\n<!-- MAT-VISUAL: V16 -->\n```\n\n---\n\n# 29. Equations and Governing Principles\n\n| Property / Process | Principle IDs |\n|---|---|\n| | |\n\n---\n\n# 30. Calculations\n\n---\n\n# 31. Experiments and Replication\n\n---\n\n# 32. Evidence and Confidence\n\n```yaml\nevidence_status: BASELINE\nconfidence: U\nreplication: NOT-ASSESSED\nunresolved_conflicts: []\n```\n\n---\n\n# 33. Sources\n\n- [PubChem periodic table download](https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/periodictable/JSON), retained 2026-09-08 as PUBCHEM-PERIODIC.\n- [CIAAW standard atomic weights](https://www.ciaaw.org/atomic-weights.htm), retained 2026-09-08 as CIAAW-2024.\n- Catalogue snapshot hashes and property-level evidence are recorded in data/catalog/sources and data/catalog/elements-baseline.json.\n\n---\n\n# 34. People and Intellectual Lineage\n\n---\n\n# 35. Open Questions\n\n---\n\n# 36. MAT / Causali E Research Notes\n\n```text\nHYPOTHESIS\nSPECULATION\nTESTABLE\nSUPPORTED\nNOT-SUPPORTED\n```\n\n---\n\n# 37. Completeness\n\n```yaml\nidentity: CURATED\nnuclear: PARTIAL # NUBASE2020 reference available; later research and curation pending\nquantum: PLANNED\nspectral: PLANNED\nelectrical: PLANNED\nmagnetic: PLANNED\nthermal: PLANNED\nmechanical: PLANNED\nchemical: PLANNED\nmaterials: PLANNED\nprocess: PLANNED\nenvironment: PLANNED\napplications: PLANNED\nsafety: PLANNED\nsources: PLANNED\nvisuals: PLANNED\n```\n\n---\n\n# 38. Revision History\n\n| Version | Date | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1.0.0 | 2026-09-08 | Initial baseline scaffold (superseded numeric claims; retained in Git history) |\n\n| 1.1.0 | 2026-09-08 | Source-backed baseline correction: PubChem/CIAAW, null semantics, prediction labels |\n\n## Evaluated nuclear data and review\n\nThe [NUBASE2020 nuclear state catalogue](0117-Tennessine-Ts-Nuclear-Evaluation.md) provides 4 evaluated states with uncertainties, qualifiers and source-line provenance. This dated evaluation does not make the whole material record complete.\n",
